tai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\", trust_remote_code=True)\nL73:     messages = [\nL74:         {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Who are you?\"},\nL75:     ]\nL76:     pipe(messages)\nL77: \nL78:     # pip install -U transformers accelerate\nL79:     # Load model directly\nL80:     from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM\nL81:     model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\", trust_remote_code=True, device_map=\"auto\")\nL82:   * Inference\nL83:   * Inference Providers\nL84:   * cite40†HuggingChat L85:   * Notebooks\nL86:   * cite41†Google Colab L87:   * cite42†Kaggle L88:   * Local Apps cite43†Settings L89:   * cite44†vLLM L90: \nL91: How to use moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905 with vLLM:\nL92: ##### Install from pip and serve model\nL93: \nL94:     # Install vLLM from pip:\nL95:     pip install vllm\nL96:     # Start the vLLM server:\nL97:     vllm serve \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\"\nL98:     # Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\nL99:     curl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\nL100:     \t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\nL101:     \t--data '{\nL102:     \t\t\"model\": \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\",\nL103:     \t\t\"messages\": [\nL104:     \t\t\t{\nL105:     \t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\nL106:     \t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\nL107:     \t\t\t}\nL108:     \t\t]\nL109:     \t}'\nL110: ##### Use Docker\nL111: \nL112:     docker model run hf.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\nL113: \nL114:   * cite45†SGLang L115: \nL116: How to use moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905 with SGLang:\nL117: ##### Install from pip and serve model\nL118: \nL119:     # Install SGLang from pip:\nL120:     pip install sglang\nL121:     # Start the SGLang server:\nL122:     python3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\nL123:         --model-path \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\" \\\nL124:         --host 0.0.0.0 \\\nL125:         --port 30000\nL126:     # Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\nL127:     curl -X POST \"http://localhost:30000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\nL128:     \t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\nL129:     \t--data '{\nL130:     \t\t\"model\": \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\",\nL131:     \t\t\"messages\": [\nL132:     \t\t\t{\nL133:     \t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\nL134:     \t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\nL135:     \t\t\t}\nL136:     \t\t]\nL137:     \t}'\nL138: ##### Use Docker images\nL139: \nL140:     docker run --gpus all \\\nL141:         --shm-size 32g \\\nL142:         -p 30000:30000 \\\nL143:         -v ~/.cache/huggingface:/root/.cache/huggingface \\\nL144:         --env \"HF_TOKEN=<secret>\" \\\nL145:         --ipc=host \\\nL146:         lmsysorg/sglang:latest \\\nL147:         python3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\nL148:             --model-path \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\" \\\nL149:             --host 0.0.0.0 \\\nL150:             --port 30000\nL151:     # Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\nL152:     curl -X POST \"http://localhost:30000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\nL153:     \t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\nL154:     \t--data '{\nL155:     \t\t\"model\": \"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\",\nL156:     \t\t\"messages\": [\nL157:     \t\t\t{\nL158:     \t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\nL159:     \t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\nL160:     \t\t\t}\nL161:     \t\t]\nL162:     \t}'\nL163:   * cite46†Docker Model Runner L164: \nL165: How to use moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905 with Docker Model Runner:\nL166: \nL167:     docker model run hf.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905\nL168: \nL169:   * cite47†Browse Quantizations to use this model in llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, or any compatible app.\nL170:   * cite48†1. Model Introduction L171:     * cite49†Key Features L172:   * cite50†2. Model Summary L173:   * cite51†3. Evaluation Results L174:   * cite52†4. Deployment L175:   * cite53†5. Model Usage L176:     * cite54†Chat Completion L177:     * cite55†Tool Calling L178:   * cite56†6. License L179:   * cite57†7. Third Party Notices L180:   * cite58†7. Contact Us L181: \nL182: cite59†Image: Kimi K2: Open Agentic Intellignece L183: \nL184: * * *\nL185: \nL186: 📰  cite60†Tech Blog†moonshotai.github.io |     📄  cite61†Paper†github.com L187: ## 1. Model Introduction\nL188: \nL189: Kimi K2-Instruct-0905 is the latest, most capable version of Kimi K2. It is a state-of-the-art mixture-of-experts (MoE) language model, featuring 32 billion activated parameters and a total of 1 trillion parameters.\nL190: ### Key Features\nL191: \nL192:   * Enhanced agentic coding intelligence: Kimi K2-Instruct-0905 demonstrates significant improvements in performance on public benchmarks and real-world coding agent tasks.\nL193:   * Improved frontend coding experience: Kimi K2-Instruct-0905 offers advancements in both the aesthetics and practicality of frontend programming.\nL194:   * Extended context length: Kimi K2-Instruct-0905’s context window has been increased from 128k to 256k tokens, providing better support for long-horizon tasks.\nL195: ## 2. Model Summary\nL196: \nL197:  |\nL198: --- | ---\nL199: Architecture  | Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)\nL200: Total Parameters  | 1T\nL201: Activated Parameters  | 32B\nL202: Number of Layers (Dense layer included)  | 61\nL203: Number of Dense Layers  | 1\nL204: Attention Hidden Dimension  | 7168\nL205: MoE Hidden Dimension (per Expert)  | 2048\nL206: Number of Attention Heads  | 64\nL207: Number of Experts  | 384\nL208: Selected Experts per Token  | 8\nL209: Number of Shared Experts  | 1\nL210: Vocabulary Size  | 160K\nL211: Context Length  | 256K\nL212: Attention Mechanism  | MLA\nL213: Activation Function  | SwiGLU\nL214: ## 3. Evaluation Results\nL215: Benchmark  | Metric  | K2-Instruct-0905  | K2-Instruct-0711  | Qwen3-Coder-480B-A35B-Instruct  | GLM-4.5  | DeepSeek-V3.1  | Claude-Sonnet-4  | Claude-Opus-4\nL216: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL217: SWE-Bench verified  | ACC  | 69.2 ± 0.63  | 65.8  | 69.6*  | 64.2*  | 66.0*  | 72.7*  | 72.5*\nL218: SWE-Bench Multilingual  | ACC  | 55.9 ± 0.72  | 47.3  | 54.7*  | 52.7  | 54.5*  | 53.3*  | -\nL219: Multi-SWE-Bench  | ACC  | 33.5 ± 0.28  | 31.3  | 32.7  | 31.7  | 29.0  | 35.7  | -\nL220: Terminal-Bench  | ACC  | 44.5 ± 2.03  | 37.5  | 37.5*  | 39.9*  | 31.3*  | 36.4*  | 43.2*\nL221: SWE-Dev  | ACC  | 66.6 ± 0.72  | 61.9  | 64.7  | 63.2  | 53.3  | 67.1  | -\nL222: All K2-Instruct-0905 numbers are reported as mean ± std over five independent, full-test-set runs. Before each run we prune the repository so that every Git object unreachable from the target commit disappears; this guarantees the agent sees only the code that would legitimately be available at that point in history.\nL223: Except for Terminal-Bench (Terminus-2), every result was produced with our in-house evaluation harness. The harness is derived from SWE-agent, but we clamp the context windows of the Bash and Edit tools and rewrite the system prompt to match the task semantics. All baseline figures denoted with an asterisk (*) are excerpted directly from their official report or public leaderboard; the remaining metrics were evaluated by us under conditions identical to those used for K2-Instruct-0905.\nL224: For SWE-Dev we go one step further: we overwrite the original repository files and delete any test file that exercises the functions the agent is expected to generate, eliminating any indirect hints about the desired implementation.\nL225: ## 4. Deployment\nL226: \nL227: > You can access Kimi K2's API on cite62†https://platform.moonshot.ai†platform.moonshot.ai , we provide OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible API for you.\nL228: >\nL229: > The Anthropic-compatible API maps temperature by `real_temperature = request_temperature * 0.6` for better compatible with existing applications.\nL230: \nL231: Our model checkpoints are stored in the block-fp8 format, you can find it on cite63†Huggingface .\nL232: \nL233: Currently, Kimi-K2 is recommended to run on the following inference engines:\nL234:   * vLLM\nL235:   * SGLang\nL236:   * KTransformers\nL237:   * TensorRT-LLM\nL238: \nL239: Deployment examples for vLLM and SGLang can be found in the cite64†Model Deployment Guide .\nL240: \nL241: * * *\nL242: ## 5. Model Usage\nL243: ### Chat Completion\nL244: Once the local inference service is up, you can interact with it through the chat endpoint:\nL245: \nL246:     `def simple_chat(client: OpenAI, model_name: str):\nL247:         messages = [\nL248:             {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.\"},\nL249:             {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Please give a brief self-introduction.\"}]},\nL250:         ]\nL251:         response = client.chat.completions.create(\nL252:             model=model_name,\nL253:             messages=messages,\nL254:             stream=False,\nL255:             temperature=0.6,\nL256:             max_tokens=256\nL257:         )\nL258:         print(response.choices[0].message.content)\nL259:     `\nL260: > The recommended temperature for Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905 is `temperature = 0.6`. If no special instructions are required, the system prompt above is a good default.\nL261: \nL262: * * *\nL263: ### Tool Calling\nL264: \nL265: Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905 has strong tool-calling capabilities. To enable them, you need to pass the list of available tools in each request, then the model will autonomously decide when and how to invoke them.\nL266: The following example demonstrates calling a weather tool end-to-end:\nL267: \nL268:     `# Your tool implementation\nL269:     def get_weather(city: str) -> dict:\nL270:         return {\"weather\": \"Sunny\"}\nL271:     # Tool schema definition\nL272:     tools = [{\nL273:         \"type\": \"function\",\nL274:         \"function\": {\nL275:             \"name\": \"get_weather\",\nL276:             \"description\": \"Retrieve current weather information. Call this when the user asks about the weather.\",\nL277:             \"parameters\": {\nL278:                 \"type\": \"object\",\nL279:                 \"required\": [\"city\"],\nL280:                 \"properties\": {\nL281:                     \"city\": {\nL282:                         \"type\": \"string\",\nL283:                         \"description\": \"Name of the city\"\nL284:                     }\nL285:                 }\nL286:             }\nL287:         }\nL288:     }]\nL289:     # Map tool names to their implementations\nL290:     tool_map = {\nL291:         \"get_weather\": get_weather\nL292:     }\nL293:     def tool_call_with_client(client: OpenAI, model_name: str):\nL294:         messages = [\nL295:             {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.\"},\nL296:             {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather like in Beijing today? Use the tool to check.\"}\nL297:         ]\nL298:         finish_reason = None\nL299:         while finish_reason is None or finish_reason == \"tool_calls\":\nL300:             completion = client.chat.completions.create(\nL301:                 model=model_name,\nL302:                 messages=messages,\nL303:                 temperature=0.6,\nL304:                 tools=tools,          # tool list defined above\nL305:                 tool_choice=\"auto\"\nL306:             )\nL307:             choice = completion.choices[0]\nL308:             finish_reason = choice.finish_reason\nL309:             if finish_reason == \"tool_calls\":\nL310:                 messages.append(choice.message)\nL311:                 for tool_call in choice.message.tool_calls:\nL312:                     tool_call_name = tool_call.function.name\nL313:                     tool_call_arguments = json.loads(tool_call.function.arguments)\nL314:                     tool_function = tool_map[tool_call_name]\nL315:                     tool_result = tool_function(**tool_call_arguments)\nL316:                     print(\"tool_result:\", tool_result)\nL317:                     messages.append({\nL318:                         \"role\": \"tool\",\nL319:                         \"tool_call_id\": tool_call.id,\nL320:                         \"name\": tool_call_name,\nL321:                         \"content\": json.dumps(tool_result)\nL322:                     })\nL323:         print(\"-\" * 100)\nL324:         print(choice.message.content)\nL325:     `\nL326: The `tool_call_with_client` function implements the pipeline from user query to tool execution. This pipeline requires the inference engine to support Kimi-K2’s native tool-parsing logic. For more information, see the cite65†Tool Calling Guide .\nL327: \nL328: * * *\nL329: ## 6. License\nL330: \nL331: Both the code repository and the model weights are released under the cite66†Modified MIT License .\nL332: \nL333: * * *\nL334: \nL335: ## 7. Third Party Notices\nL336: \nL337: See cite67†THIRD PARTY NOTICES L338: \nL339: * * *\nL340: ## 7. Contact Us\nL341: \nL342: If you have any questions, please reach out at support@moonshot.cn.\nL343: \nL344: Downloads last month\nL345:     65,135\nL346: \nL347: Safetensors\nL348: \nL349: Model size\nL350: \nL351: 1T params\nL352: \nL353: Tensor type\nL354: \nL355: F32\nL356: \nL357: ·\nL358: \nL359: BF16\nL360: \nL361: ·\nL362: \nL363: F8_E4M3\nL364: \nL365: ·\nL366: \nL367: Chat template\nL368: \nL369: Files info\nL370: \nL371: Inference Providers cite68†NEW L372: \nL373: Novita\nL374: \nL375:   * cite69†Text Generation L376: \nL377: Examples\nL378: \nL379: Input a message to start chatting with moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-0905.\nL380: \nL381: [Input: Your prompt here...]\nL382: \nL383: Send\nL384: \nL385: View Code Snippets\nL386: \nL387: cite70†Compare providers L388: ## Model tree for moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Instruct-